@spec tm_curve_density_spec  src=tests/specs/tm_curve_density_spec.lua  loc=109  cases=3
@exercises midiManager (h.fm), trackerManager (h.tm)
@surface   fm:dump, tm:addEvent, tm:flush, tm:rebuild
@harness   mk

# Intent
  Curve density: what the fold puts on the wire *between* breakpoints. The sum of two curves has no
  single-breakpoint representation, so it is sampled onto the ccGridStep lattice; a curve that is the
  only thing moving across a segment does have one, and rides out as its own breakpoint. That second
  rule only holds if the fold's segments are independent of how the dirt sliced the channel, which is
  why foldChains folds over its records' extent. see design/note-macros-v2.md § The fx chain

# Helpers
  @fn note(ppq, endppq, pitch, lane, fx)  @ 13-16
  @fn pbSeats(h, lo, hi)  @ 18-27
  @fn ppqsOf(seats)  @ 29-33
  @fn overlappingPair(h)  @ 37-41
      -- Two continuous producers whose windows overlap on [120, 240): sine A alone before it, both across
      -- it, sine B alone after. One fixture covers all three of the fold's cases.

# Cases
  @case 'a lone curve seats its own breakpoints, not a lattice sampling of them'  [harness]  @ 48-61
  @case 'a sum of two curves has no breakpoint representation, so it densifies'  [harness]  @ 67-85
  @case 'the seats do not depend on how the dirt sliced the channel'  [harness]  @ 91-106

